{"id": "De8JhVzouDJ", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "🐭🦉🫏 Can you guess which god or goddess rides each of these animals?\n\nThree rounds, from easy to tricky! Most people get the first two… but will you get all three? 👀\n\nIn Hindu traditions, many gods and goddesses have a vahana — an animal or creature associated with them.\n\n🐭 Round 1: Mooshak, the mouse, is Lord Ganesha’s vahana.\n\n🦉 Round 2: The owl is Maa Lakshmi’s vahana.\n\n🫏 Round 3: The donkey is Maa Kalaratri’s vahana, the seventh form of Maa Durga. Her dhyana mantra describes her as Kharāsthitā — seated on a donkey.\n\nHow many did you get right — 1, 2, or all 3? Tell us in the comments! 👇\n\n📚 Want to introduce your little ones to these stories? Explore our Navadurga Series picture books at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\nBooks 1–3 are available as a set for ₹500, and Book 7, Maa Kalaratri, is coming soon! ❤️\n\n💾 Save this for a quiz with your kids, and share it with someone who thinks they know it all!\n\n#RishiKatha #Ganesha #MaaLakshmi #MaaKalaratri #Navadurga MaaDurga Vahana IndianHeritage KidsBooks IndianParents StorytimeForKids QuizTime", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792979734, "like_count": 446, "comment_count": 16, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1669399951480895a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 27.178, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPhsa5_ZcsOwtiITAz_mAoTOxPS6iEGaiEGa_wXx4zfyGauWfuqsjKA4FY3I5SHrMP2tSbrYA8hbSS2YTEythTWtfKYRoVQ_QUYxZs.mp4?_nc_cat=111&_nc_oc=AdpDnhzdysLQDcSgQgPDXzCaMGtTa-3I52zGJPRm9ChQam5ME2Ce389i8l7QY-B31iFqAHEeoJYJ5E5p5D6s9In0&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=9cApy62iZrQQ7kNvwGF-Lns&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=hGipnyzNTnCkohFWzxeBLA&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_